                         for CSG that incorporates explicit phoneme-level condi-\n                                         els [2–5] excel at high-fidelity generation but lack fine-\n                                                                                                                   tioning inspired by research on SVS. Specifically, we note\n                                         grained structural control. In contrast, SVS systems [6–8]\n                                                                                                                   that SVS models such as FastSpeech [9] employ a module\n                                         offer precise melody and phoneme control but are limited\n                                                                                                                   named “duration predictor” to predict the physical tempo-\n                                         to isolated vocals. CSG demands seamless integration of\n                                                                                                                   ral duration of each phoneme in the lyrics, and a module\n                                                                                                                   named “length regulator” (LR) to enforce such timing con-\n                                                      © Wei-Jaw Lee, Hsuan-Yu Yeh, Ting-Yi Hu, Chih-Pin Tan,       ditioning on the generative process, so that the onset and\n                                         Fang-Duo Tsai and Yi-Hsuan Yang. Licensed under a Creative Commons        offset of each sung phoneme can be accurately controlled.\n                                         Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0). Attribution: Wei-      We recognize that such precise temporal alignment of lin-\n                                         Jaw Lee, Hsuan-Yu Yeh, Ting-Yi Hu, Chih-Pin Tan, Fang-Duo Tsai and        guistic conten