{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bb3ddab72f8da3ca", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# InstructAudio: Unified speech and music generation with natural language instruction\narXiv: 2511.18487\nAuthors: Chunyu Qiang, Kang Yin, Xiaopeng Wang, Yuzhe Liang, Jiahui Zhao, Ruibo Fu, Tianrui Wang, Cheng Gong, Chen Zhang, Longbiao Wang, Jianwu Dang\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We introduce a joint modeling framework for speech and music generation based on a multimodal diffusion transformer architecture.\n  2. We achieve unified text-based control over speech and music generation through a standardized instruction-phoneme input format encompassing timbre, paralinguistic, and musical attributes while supporting dialogue generation.\n  3. Experimental results demonstrate state-of-the-art performance in instruction-based text-to-speech while maintaining competitive text-to-music capabilities.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-NL描述, TTS/控制-指令合成, 压缩, 压缩/量化-VAE\n===\n# UniSonate: A Unified Model for Speech, Music, and Sound Effect Generation with Text Instructions\narXiv: 2604.22209\nAuthors: \nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose UniSonate, the first flow-matching framework to unify TTS, TTM, and TTA tasks under a consistent, reference-free natural language instruction interface.\n  2. We introduce Dynamic Token Injection, a mechanism that symbolically represents unstructured acoustic events, enabling precise duration control for sound effects within a phoneme-driven architecture.\n  3. Extensive experiments demonstrate that UniSonate achieves state-of-the-art performance in instruction-based TTS and TTM while exhibiting positive transfer where joint training enhances structural coherence and prosodic expressiveness over single-task baselines.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-NL描述, TTS/功能-多任务统一", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "6ef7fb18-4d32-4ca0-9f52-0d6e077d7474", "uuid": "b76d1b56-0e21-4053-acd7-71bedd8436fe", "timestamp": "2026-07-30T07:12:00.387Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# InstructAudio: Unified speech and music generation with natural language instruction\narXiv: 2511.18487\nAuthors: Chunyu Qiang, Kang Yin, Xiaopeng Wang, Yuzhe Liang, Jiahui Zhao, Ruibo Fu, Tianrui Wang, Cheng Gong, Chen Zhang, Longbiao Wang, Jianwu Dang\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We introduce a joint modeling framework for speech and music generation based on a multimodal diffusion transformer architecture.\n  2. We achieve unified text-based control over speech and music generation through a standardized instruction-phoneme input format encompassing timbre, paralinguistic, and musical attributes while supporting dialogue generation.\n  3. Experimental results demonstrate state-of-the-art performance in instruction-based text-to-speech while maintaining competitive text-to-music capabilities.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-NL描述, TTS/控制-指令合成, 压缩, 压缩/量化-VAE\n===\n# UniSonate: A Unified Model for Speech, Music, and Sound Effect Generation with Text Instructions\narXiv: 2604.22209\nAuthors: \nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose UniSonate, the first flow-matching framework to unify TTS, TTM, and TTA tasks under a consistent, reference-free natural language instruction interface.\n  2. We introduce Dynamic Token Injection, a mechanism that symbolically represents unstructured acoustic events, enabling precise duration control for sound effects within a phoneme-driven architecture.\n  3. Extensive experiments demonstrate that UniSonate achieves state-of-the-art performance in instruction-based TTS and TTM while exhibiting positive transfer where joint training enhances structural coherence and prosodic expressiveness over single-task baselines.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-NL描述, TTS/功能-多任务统一", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
